 r←{noAPLnames}StashListContent(projectID n);rc;more;path;⎕TRAP;space;cmd;data;hasUntrackedFiles
⍝ Lists all files, tracked and untracked, in a stash.
⍝ Specify projectID and the stash number via ⍵.
⍝ `projectID` must be one of:\\
⍝   * Fully qualified name of a namespace that is managed by Git
⍝   * Path to a Git-managed project\\
⍝ `n` is the number of the stash.\\
 ⎕TRAP←(811 'E' '⎕DMX.EM ⎕signal 811')(0 'N')
 noAPLnames←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ 0}'noAPLnames'
 (space path)←EstablishProject projectID
 r←''

⍝ First we need to find out whether untracked files were actually captured.
 cmd←'log -1 --format=%P stash@{',(⍕n),'}'
 (rc more data)←path U.RunGitCommand cmd
 more U.Assert 0=rc
 ((≢'fatal:')↓more)U.Assert'fatal:'{⍺≢(≢⍺)↑⍵}more
 data←' '(≠⊆⊢)⊃,/data
 hasUntrackedFiles←3=≢data

 cmd←'stash show --name-only ',(hasUntrackedFiles/'-u '),'stash@{',(⍕n),'}'
 (rc more r)←path U.RunGitCommand cmd
 :If ∨/'No stash entries found'⍷∊more
     r←''
 :Else
     more U.Assert 0=rc
     ((≢'fatal:')↓more)U.Assert'fatal:'{⍺≢(≢⍺)↑⍵}more
 :EndIf
 r←(F.AddTrailingSep path)∘,¨r
 :If ~noAPLnames
     r←⍪r
     r,←⊂''
     r[;2]←space∘{⎕NEXISTS ⍵:⍺ GetItemName ⍵ ⋄ ''}¨,r[;1]
 :EndIf
